# scripts/.sensitive-needles.example — FORMAT DOCUMENTATION ONLY.
#
# Every entry below is SYNTHETIC. Never put a real name, organisation, or
# project in this file: it is TRACKED and this repo is PUBLIC. A denylist of
# sensitive strings is itself a disclosure of those strings.
#
# Setup:
#   cp scripts/.sensitive-needles.example scripts/.sensitive-needles
#   # then replace these placeholders with the real strings
#
# scripts/.sensitive-needles is gitignored. pre-commit-guard.sh reads it and
# REFUSES to run (exit 1) if it is missing or empty — it fails closed rather
# than silently passing.
#
# FORMAT
#   - one needle per line
#   - blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored
#   - leading/trailing spaces are part of the needle, so don't add any
#   - matching is SUBSTRING and CASE-INSENSITIVE (grep -Fi), NOT a regex:
#     '.', '*', '(' etc. are literal characters
#   - matching is NOT diacritic-folded. "Grünwald" will NOT match
#     "Grunwald". List BOTH spellings of any name with a diacritic variant.
#   - list the space-stripped/case-folded form too if the string appears
#     mangled inside identifiers or fixture ids (e.g. "exampleorgname")
#   - do NOT hash these. See the long comment in pre-commit-guard.sh: hashes
#     only match whole-string exact equality, which breaks substring and
#     case-insensitive matching and would make the guard silently pass.

# --- synthetic people -------------------------------------------------------
Jane Placeholder
Sample Testperson
Example Grunwald
Example Grünwald

# --- synthetic organisations ------------------------------------------------
ExampleOrgName
exampleorgname
Placeholder Foundation
Sample Institute International

# --- synthetic project / product names --------------------------------------
Fictional Project Alpha
"fictional project alpha"
